  "description": "FILGIS crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n m c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H66 Cr2 Dy3 N10 O29 9+,9(Cl1 O4 1-),15(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1M (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.470-4.088 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.13-111.36°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3Cr2(HGly)6(dpyo)2(μ3-OH)6(H2O)7]·(ClO4)9·15H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
